WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.120
Six layouts, one system.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.404
Your floor plan decides the shape, not the furniture.

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:10.435
Standard benches only line up in rows.

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:16.487
But real cells need corners, islands and back-to-back stations to fit the space and the flow.

00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:23.640
Flexi starter and adder sections share double-sided columns, so they can be arranged in six ways:

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:30.126
in-line for a straight flow, back-to-back to share columns, U for a compact cell, L for corners,

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:33.774
T for a branching process, and X for a central island.

00:00:34.054 --> 00:00:39.059
Because sections share columns, you can also change from one layout to another later,

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:40.590
instead of starting again.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:47.053
One EV-charger R&D lab seats 12 engineers back to back on Furnisys Flexi.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:53.901
A jewellery maker doubled from 5 to 10 operators by converting its in-line Flexi to back-to-back,

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.947
adding only a work surface and a few shelves.

00:00:57.547 --> 00:01:01.329
So when your team grows, reshape the line instead of replacing it.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:03.132
Which layout fits your floor?

00:01:03.412 --> 00:01:07.742
Comment below, and next, learn how to retrofit the bench you already have.

00:01:08.342 --> 00:01:12.587
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

